# ============================================================================
#  HB Briefing - topics.txt
# ============================================================================
#  Standing topics are the fastest way to retarget the monitor. Add a subject,
#  and HB Briefing treats it as always relevant: matching items are flagged even
#  when no enforcement, filing or litigation language appears, they are graded
#  at the interest level you give them, and the AI is told to prioritise them.
#
#  Unless "Search Google News for each topic" is switched off in Settings, each
#  active topic also becomes its own Google News query feed, so a subject works
#  without adding a single RSS URL.
#
#  LINE FORMAT - three forms, each a superset of the one above it:
#
#      Broadband overbuild                      subject only (medium interest)
#      Broadband overbuild | high               subject + interest level
#      Broadband overbuild | high | Telecom     subject + level + group
#
#  Interest level:  high | medium | low
#      high    a hit is briefed near the top; treat as a headline matter
#      medium  a hit is briefed normally (default)
#      low     a hit is kept and reported, but ranked below other signals
#
#  GROUPS - a comment beginning with ## opens a group:
#
#      ## Telecom and broadband
#      fiber overbuild
#      municipal broadband
#
#  Everything below a heading belongs to that group until the next heading, so a
#  whole area can be switched on or off by uncommenting a block. Groups are shown
#  in the briefing, in reports and in the GUI topic editor.
#
#  Everything below is commented out on purpose: the file ships as a library you
#  can switch on a block at a time, so a fresh install never starts by fetching a
#  hundred feeds. Uncomment what you want, then run a scan.
#
#  Limits: 150 active topics, the first 20 also become Google News feeds.
#  A topic is matched at a word start, so "chip fab" matches "chip fabs" but the
#  topic "AI" will not match the word "said".
# ============================================================================


